ng to  recover from a two-year long drought  that ended in 2017 nomadic pastoralism  has been a way of life for millions of  Somalis for centuries but the droughts  are threatening but many of the  displaced say they now have no farms or  had to go back to and it's unlikely many  of them will ever return Mohammed Al  Jazeera Baidoa in southwest Somali
 

